      "edition": "Sunday 11 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching change",
          "heading": "Fiji part ways with coach Mick Byrne eighteen months before World Cup",
          "body": "Fiji Rugby ended Mick Byrne's tenure in April, with the Australian leaving \"by mutual agreement\" 18 months before the World Cup. Byrne had been in charge since 2024, after a stint at Fijian Drua, and his reign included wins over Scotland, Wales and Japan. AFP reported he appeared to have had a difference of opinion with management over future plans, and Fiji Rugby framed the move as necessary for the programme to follow its new direction."
        },
