      "edition": "Sunday 11 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad absences",
          "heading": "Dupont, Ntamack and Ramos missed France's July opener against New Zealand",
          "body": "Dupont, Ntamack, Ramos, Alldritt and Bielle-Biarrey were all missing from Fabien Galthié's squad for the July opener, the first Nations Championship test, against New Zealand in Christchurch. Many of the absences were put down to workload after the long Top 14 season, leaving a younger France group to face a formidable road opponent. The team's Nations Championship record now stands at two wins from three, including 42-15 over Japan in Round 3."
        },
