        {
          "kicker": "Concussion case",
          "heading": "World Rugby and UK bodies lose bid to dismiss brain injury claims",
          "body": "The concussion litigation remains open, with the claimants facing a £2.8m legal bill to continue, as the Guardian reported earlier this week. The latest ruling reported came in late August: World Rugby and UK bodies lost a bid to have the brain injury cases thrown out of court. No coverage of a further move appeared in today's press, so the case stays open until the fees are settled or the claims resolved."
        },
        {
