      "edition": "Sunday 11 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Forwards appointment",
          "heading": "Mario Ledesma returns as Argentina forwards coach until 2027 World Cup",
          "body": "Mario Ledesma is back in the Argentina set-up, taking charge of the forwards until the end of next year's World Cup in Australia, as the Union confirmed alongside Shaun Edwards' appointment. The 53-year-old former hooker played 84 Tests between 1996 and 2011 and was Argentina's head coach from 2018 to 2022. \"I am honoured and very grateful for the opportunity to work with Los Pumas again,\" he said. Before this he worked as a consultant and at U17 level."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Fiji part ways with coach Mick Byrne by mutual agreement",
