    "461": {
      "date": "2026-10-11",
      "edition": "Sunday 11 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Rankings fallout",
          "heading": "Wallabies hold sixth in world rankings, just 0.11 clear of Scotland",
          "body": "The Eden Park loss has cost the Wallabies ground in the World Rugby rankings. They drop from 85.55 to 84.89 points and hold sixth, just 0.11 clear of Scotland in seventh. Australia could have climbed to fourth, their highest ranking since November 2021, with a win by more than 15 points, but the 31-point defeat left them chasing. The All Blacks rose to 91.81, now just over a point behind South Africa on 93.09. Another defeat in Sydney on Saturday would see the Wallabies slip behind Scotland."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Fiji part ways with coach Mick Byrne by mutual agreement",
          "body": "Japan's domestic League One reverses eligibility curbs after court settlement. South Africa's Bulls thrash Lions 57-15 in URC."
        }
      ],
